& [ObservedFailure]
  + the P0 twenty-GiB startup threshold admitted a clean WSL workspace build that expanded its non-sparse dynamic virtual disk until the Windows system volume approached zero free space
  + cleaning the exact WSL Cargo target released internal filesystem blocks but did not immediately return their backing allocation to Windows
  + a later native-Windows workspace build began with approximately twenty-seven GiB free and reached effectively zero while linking a test PDB
  + the linker returned LNK1318 FILE_SYSTEM before that test executed
  + exact Cargo cleanup restored host capacity and no source or user data was deleted

& [ContractGap]
  + P0 checks capacity only at startup and cannot stop an admitted child before the reserve is consumed
  + P0 compiles default test and development debug information and permits incremental artifacts whose storage is not required for semantic verification
  + P0 plan-only mode throws below its execution threshold even though the canonical contract says plan-only invokes neither WSL nor Cargo
  + the offline contract test consequently refuses to run when the machine is most in need of a read-only diagnostic plan
  + one fixed minimum threshold does not distinguish admission headroom from the reserve that must remain available throughout execution

& [DevelopmentNeed]
  + keep the default operation read-only plan-only and successful at any observable capacity
  + expose current free bytes startup minimum reserve floor capacity status and exact command in the JSON plan
  + enforce startup capacity only when Execute is selected so an impossible threshold can prove pre-child refusal safely
  + disable Cargo incremental output and test or development debug information for the verification lane
  + poll the Windows repository volume from the WSL child while Cargo runs
  + interrupt the admitted Cargo child and return a distinct capacity-guard status before free space crosses the caller-visible reserve
  + retain one build job one test thread stable target stable temporary directory no automatic cleanup and no remote or OneDrive behavior

& [SelectedPrototype]
  + evolve the existing entry point to profile cantor-bounded-workspace-verification/0.2
  + retain MinimumFreeGiB as startup admission and add ReserveFreeGiB plus MonitorIntervalSeconds
  + require MinimumFreeGiB to be strictly greater than ReserveFreeGiB
  + derive the WSL mount for the repository volume from its exact Windows drive identity
  + run Cargo as one background child inside a Bash guard loop that samples available bytes and sends interrupt on reserve breach
  + render plan Bash without invoking WSL and test the exact guard text with isolated PowerShell child processes

& [Boundary]
  + no cache deletion compaction sparse-mode mutation WSL configuration remote host OneDrive product runtime semantic authority or autonomous cleanup
  + no claim that lean debug settings reduce semantic test coverage
  + no claim that a startup estimate predicts final target size
  + P1 is local development verification policy and does not alter Cantor runtime behavior
